Z||000000||Fret Naught||01-08-2001||01:08 AM||||It's has been awhile since I have posted, but rest assured I have been reading, I got a new password as my email changed, and I just can't seem to memorize it!!!<P>I need some tips advice etc... My steering wheel is loose, what I mean is there is quite a bit of slop up and down, side to side, I assume that the bushings or bearings are worn, but I have no idea how to fix it or what it involves. But I do know who to ask so lets have it folks I am depending on you. thanks<BR>Fret Naught<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FretNaught_sig_16.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||01-08-2001||01:47 AM||||well......it's kinda complicated but, it can be done......the steering wheel has to be removed, the turn signal unit has to be removed and then you will find that there are three torx bolts deep inside the steering column to tighten. You will only be able to see two of them however -- once the turn signal unit is removed you will need to look deep into the holes at approximately the 4 o'clock and 8 o'clock positions. Use a torx bit on a ratchet extension -- tighten these and your steering column will be fine. These do loosen over time........if you need any further help, call me at the shop at 510-233-4376......||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||01-08-2001||01:49 AM||||oh, I forgot to mention, that is the adjustment for the steering wheel itself, if it is the column that is loose you will find two 15mm bolts and two 15mm nuts under the column that will tighten the steering column.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||01-08-2001||01:53 AM||||Would some blue Loctite on the threads be a good idea?||||reg||5
Z||000004||FieroJoe||01-08-2001||04:34 PM||||I can't see where loctite would be a problem, seems to me that it would only help.  Blue, yes, red, no.  The red stuff will probably lock it so tight that the bolt would shear if it must be removed.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||01-08-2001||07:28 PM||||The tilt unit has come loose.<P>There are a bunch of notes in my cave for the steering column. I just added a link to Oliver's site which has a pictorial of the steering column disassembly down to the lock.<P>If you've never done this kind of work before get help from someone that has. The tilt unit can hurt you if you aren't careful. Expect it to take at least a couple hours.<P>Yes. Blue locktight on the 4 aflicted bolts is fine.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||qwikgta||01-08-2001||11:11 PM||||When I got my 88 the tilt was shot, lots of play..up, down, left and right.. I went to my local parts yard and got one off an 85 GT.  It had the key in the ignition and all it took was removing the bolt at the base of the steering shaft near the brake pedal and the two bolts holding it under the dash.  I upgraded to the GT leather wheel and the tilt is tight..total cost was $40.00  Might be easier than a rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||01-08-2001||11:38 PM||||I replaced mine, just to much trouble to rebuild/fix, and the price from Fierodave<BR>for a complete plug & play column was to good to pass up. Ogre's info also made me leave it alone and get a good one, and I didn't want the Toy to be down for any time<BR>if something went worng.<P>Just a thought???<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
